# #191 Illidan mirror: a powershield returns Illidan's Eye Beam
# a (Illidan) fires its neutral special at 600 from x -240; b (Illidan) at x 240 powershields it with
# one full trigger press. A reflection sends back a's own projectile: same family (a's fighter
# code), kind and model, half damage, turned around and owned by b (the `reflect` line on b's
# trace), and at this distance it expires before reaching a. Frames are read from this script's headless farm trace.
# Syntax and checks: smashcraft:docs/native-bot-session.md.
#! chat -dev quick pair illidan / illidan
600 a tap X 2
629 b shield 1
659 b shield 0
# View held a second: a moment the parity check replays.
721 a press VIEW
791 a release VIEW
# Expected (replay of this script): b's press reflects on the frame the beam meets its shield; the
# reflected beam keeps the 7 frames it had left, too few to cross the 480 units back to a, so it strikes no one.
#! expect b 629 reflect family 2 kind 4 model Abilities\Weapons\IllidanMissile\IllidanMissile.mdx direction -1 multiplier 0.500 life 7
#! absent a 600-721 damage
#! absent b 600-721 damage
